Vendored Excalidraw collaboration client — provenance and license
=================================================================

The files in this directory (`encryption.ts`, `protocol.ts`, `Portal.ts`,
`Collab.ts`) are vendored and adapted from the Excalidraw monorepo at tag
v0.18.1 (matching the `@excalidraw/excalidraw@0.18.1` npm package this app
embeds). The npm package ships no room client; the collab client lives only
in the (unpublished, MIT-licensed) excalidraw-app. Sources:

- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/excalidraw-app/collab/Collab.tsx
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/excalidraw-app/collab/Portal.tsx
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/excalidraw-app/data/index.ts
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/excalidraw-app/app_constants.ts
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/packages/excalidraw/data/encryption.ts
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/packages/excalidraw/utils.ts (bytesToHexString)
- https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw/blob/v0.18.1/packages/excalidraw/constants.ts (IDLE/ACTIVE thresholds, ENCRYPTION_KEY_BITS)

Adaptations (documented per-file in headers): Firebase scene/file persistence
stripped (Dwellium persists via its own whiteboardStore + One Save), analytics
stripped, jotai/React-component shell replaced by a framework-free session
class, lodash.throttle replaced by a local throttle. The wire protocol
(socket.io event names, message subtypes, AES-GCM end-to-end encryption, room
link format `#room=<roomId>,<key>`) is kept byte-compatible with the official
`excalidraw/excalidraw-room` server this era of the app targets.

